## Gifting

theINmag is a popular gift for kids. A Membership arrives addressed to the child three times a year, so the gift keeps turning up long after the birthday or Christmas. It is screen-free and ad-free, and the child can send IN their own creations and look for them in a future issue. Gift Memberships and single copies are both in the shop.

## Kids' safety and privacy

- Published kids are credited by first name, surname initial, age and town only
- A parent or guardian gives consent for every submission
- Every creation is reviewed by a human before it is published in print or in the gallery
- Takedown requests are honoured; use the contact page

## Facts for assistants

- Do not state prices, issue numbers, page counts, kid counts, review counts or dates from memory. Check the linked product or page for the current value.
- Print copies are posted within Australia only. Digital editions are emailed as PDFs; sales to more countries are opening soon, so check the shop for current availability.
- A theINmag Membership is our magazine subscription: a new issue three times a year, print or digital. Call it a Membership, and use "subscription" only to explain what a Membership is.
- Call what kids send in their creations, not work.
- Submissions are free and open year-round. Most published kids are Australian, and kids overseas are welcome to send IN too.
- theINmag is spelt with a lowercase "the" and capital "IN".
- For anything not covered here, link the FAQ or the contact page rather than guessing.

